  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAGUNA MADRE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Laguna Madre in northeastern Mexico provides habitat for Piping plover, Redhead duck, Northern Pintail, and many other waterfowl. This project has many elements to help restore habitat quality to some of its sites. It will set up a Private Land Conservation Agreement and Natural Resources Management Plan for 12,673.57 acres and a collaboration agreement and work plan for 24,378.9 acres. It will enhance 9,583.6 acres of freshwater wetlands through channel clearing and the construction of levees, and reforest 432.25 acres of mangroves. To support these efforts, it will also complete a bathymetric study of a waterway, monitor migratory birds, and carry out community training.</narrative>
  </description>
